# Playwright Conventions

## Auth (from auth-strategy.md)

Stored session by default (`playwright/.auth/user.json` via `tests/auth.setup.ts` and project `storageState`); UI login only for login-page tests. Override with empty storage when the scenario must start logged out:

```typescript
test.use({ storageState: { cookies: [], origins: [] } });
```

## Page Objects (from pom-conventions)

One POM per page/component in `pages/`; locators as `readonly` in the constructor; no assertions in POMs; tests describe intent. Priority: `getByRole` → `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder` → `getByText` → `getByTestId` (comment why). Disambiguate with `.filter({ hasText })`, not `.first()`.

```typescript
// tests/foo.spec.ts — expect here
await programs.openNewProgramModal();
await expect(modal.programNameInput).toBeVisible();

// pages/ProgramsPage.ts — actions only
async openNewProgramModal() {
  await this.newProgramButton.click();
}
```

## Locators

Role/label-based; never CSS selectors or XPath; never brittle exact text when a role+name works.

## Data & cleanup (from api-cleanup)

Unique names with `Date.now()` (or similar); every test that creates a program calls `trackProgram(uuid)` and imports `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts`, not `@playwright/test`. Teardown deletes via API (`DELETE /api/programs/<uuid>?purge=true`); never delete data the test did not create.
